---
import '@fontsource-variable/inter';
import '@fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono';
import manifest from '../../../public/images/saturday-worlds/2026-10-24/manifest.json';
import journey from '../../data/saturday-worlds-journey.json';
import '../../styles/saturday-worlds.css';
const images = manifest.images;
const byId = new Map(images.map(image => [image.id, image]));
const hero = byId.get(journey.heroId)!;
const accent = byId.get(journey.accentId)!;
const brands = [...new Set(images.map(image => image.brand))];
const canonical = 'https://pointcast.xyz/saturday-worlds/';
const label = image => `${image.title} · variation ${image.variant} of 4`;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-motion="auto">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Saturday, slightly elsewhere. · PointCast</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A Saturday excursion through imagined coastal worlds: six chapters, 360 Midjourney images, and absolutely no need to find parking. October 24, 2026." />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Saturday, slightly elsewhere." />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Six chapters. 360 images. One very imaginary afternoon on the California coast." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={`https://pointcast.xyz${hero.src}`} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f4f0df" />
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/json" href="/images/saturday-worlds/2026-10-24/manifest.json" title="All 360 images and their generation provenance" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#journey">Skip to the journey</a>
    <header class="masthead">
      <a href="/" class="wordmark">PointCast<span>↗</span></a>
      <span class="issue-label">THE SATURDAY VISUAL / 01</span>
      <a href="#all-images" class="archive-jump">All 360 <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
    </header>
    <main>
      <section class="cover" aria-labelledby="cover-title">
        <div class="cover-topline"><span>Saturday, October 24, 2026 · Pacific</span><span>AI-made places. Real Saturday energy.</span></div>
        <div class="cover-heading">
          <h1 id="cover-title">Saturday,<br /><span>slightly elsewhere.</span></h1>
          <div class="date-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><span>OCT</span><strong>24</strong><span>20 — 26</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cover-art">
          <button class="image-button cover-main" data-open-image={hero.id} aria-label={`Enlarge ${label(hero)}`}>
            <img src={hero.src} srcset={`${hero.thumb} ${hero.thumbWidth}w, ${hero.src} ${hero.width}w`} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 86vw" width={hero.width} height={hero.height} alt={journey.heroAlt} fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
            <span class="image-corner">LOOK A LITTLE CLOSER ↗</span>
          </button>
          <div class="cover-postcard"><button class="image-button" data-open-image={accent.id} aria-label={`Enlarge ${label(accent)}`}><img src={accent.thumb} width={accent.width} height={accent.height} alt={journey.accentAlt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></button><span>Wish you were<br /><em>somewhere like this.</em></span></div>
          <div class="cover-number">360<span>ways to wander</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cover-intro"><p>A courtyard with no calendar invites. A tiny vehicle with big weekend plans. A whole coast that took a turn toward the possible.</p><div><p>Come for a six-stop afternoon. Stay for every strange, sunny variation.</p><a class="primary-link" href="#chapter-1">Take the scenic route <span>↓</span></a></div></div>
        <p class="small-note">An imagined South Bay, generated with Midjourney. These places, products and campaigns are speculative concepts. Nothing here is a property listing, built project, real offer or endorsement.</p>
      </section>
      <nav class="journey-bar" aria-label="Journey chapters">
        <div class="journey-status"><span id="worlds-progress-label">Your afternoon / 6 stops</span><progress id="worlds-progress" max="100" value="0" aria-label="Journey progress"></progress></div>
        <div class="chapter-links">{journey.chapters.map((chapter, i) => <a href={`#chapter-${i + 1}`} data-chapter-link={`chapter-${i + 1}`} aria-label={`Chapter ${i + 1}: ${chapter.title}`}>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}<span>{chapter.shortTitle}</span></a>)}</div>
        <button id="worlds-motion" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Reduce motion</button>
      </nav>
      <div id="journey">
        {journey.chapters.map((chapter, index) => <section class={`chapter chapter-${index + 1}`} id={`chapter-${index + 1}`} data-worlds-chapter={chapter.shortTitle} aria-labelledby={`chapter-title-${index + 1}`}>
          <header class="chapter-heading"><span class="chapter-number">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><p class="eyebrow">{chapter.kicker}</p><h2 id={`chapter-title-${index + 1}`}>{chapter.title}</h2><p>{chapter.intro}</p></div><span class="chapter-direction" aria-hidden="true">↘</span></header>
          <div class="chapter-pictures">{chapter.images.map((pick, position) => { const item = byId.get(pick.id)!; return <figure class={position === 0 ? 'journey-picture lead-picture' : 'journey-picture'}><button class="image-button" data-open-image={item.id} aria-label={`Enlarge ${label(item)}`}><img src={position === 0 ? item.src : item.thumb} srcset={`${item.thumb} ${item.thumbWidth}w, ${item.src} ${item.width}w`} sizes={position === 0 ? '(max-width: 700px) 96vw, 74vw' : '(max-width: 600px) 88vw, 29vw'} width={item.width} height={item.height} alt={pick.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><span class="image-corner">{item.category.startsWith('ad') ? 'CAMPAIGN CONCEPT' : 'IMAGINED WORLD'} ↗</span></button><figcaption><div><span class="picture-index">{String(index * 4 + position + 1).padStart(2, '0')} / 24</span><h3>{pick.caption}</h3></div><p>{pick.note}</p><span class="source-label">{item.title} · {item.brand}{item.category === 'ad-selected' ? ' · selected ad representative' : ''}</span>{item.headline && <p class="ad-exact-copy"><span>CAMPAIGN COPY</span>“{item.headline}”<small>{item.shortCopy}</small></p>}</figcaption></figure>})}</div>
          <div class="chapter-outro"><span>{chapter.outro}</span><a href={index === 5 ? '#all-images' : `#chapter-${index + 2}`}>{index === 5 ? 'Open the whole contact sheet' : 'Keep wandering'} <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        </section>)}
      </div>
      <section class="intermission" aria-labelledby="detour-title"><span class="detour-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><p class="eyebrow">A very small detour</p><h2 id="detour-title">Let the afternoon<br />pick for you.</h2><p>One image from all 360. Could be a courtyard. Could be a pocket-sized harbor. The odds are pleasantly weird.</p><button type="button" id="worlds-surprise" class="primary-link">Take a chance on a view <span>↗</span></button></div></section>
      <section class="archive-section" id="all-images" aria-labelledby="all-images-title">
        <header class="archive-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">The complete Saturday contact sheet</p><h2 id="all-images-title">Nothing left<br />on the cutting-room floor.</h2></div><div class="archive-total">360<span>actual generated images</span></div></header>
        <p class="archive-dek">100 coastal images + 100 South Bay scenes + 160 ad images. The ads represent <strong>40 distinct concepts</strong>: 40 selected representatives and 120 alternate variations. Every original has a web-optimized image here. Tap any image to see all four variations.</p>
        <div class="archive-filters">
          <label class="search-label">Find a little world<input id="worlds-search" type="search" placeholder="Try courtyard, garden, harbor…" autocomplete="off" /></label>
          <label>Collection<select id="worlds-category"><option value="all">Everything · 360</option><option value="coastal">Coastal futures · 100</option><option value="scene">South Bay scenes · 100</option><option value="ad-selected">Selected ads · 40 concepts</option><option value="ad-alternate">Alternate ad variations · 120</option></select></label>
          <label>World<select id="worlds-brand"><option value="all">Every world</option>{brands.map(brand => <option value={brand}>{brand}</option>)}</select></label>
          <button id="worlds-reset" type="button">Reset</button>
        </div>
        <div class="archive-status"><p id="worlds-count" aria-live="polite">360 images to explore</p><a href="/saturday-worlds/contact-sheet/">Simple all-images view ↗</a></div>
        <div id="worlds-gallery" class="worlds-gallery"></div>
        <button type="button" id="worlds-more" class="load-more">Show more views ↓</button>
        <noscript><p><a href="/saturday-worlds/contact-sheet/">Browse all 360 images in the complete static contact sheet.</a></p></noscript>
      </section>
      <section class="colophon" aria-labelledby="colophon-title"><h2 id="colophon-title">A note from the imaginary coast.</h2><div><p>This feature brings together two requested Midjourney batches made on October 24, 2026: <em>Pacific Common Futures</em> and <em>South Bay Worlds</em>. The original outputs were generated with Midjourney V8.2; these are locally optimized copies, with the original job IDs and file fingerprints preserved in the <a href="/images/saturday-worlds/2026-10-24/manifest.json">image record</a>.</p><p>The South Bay worlds explore PointCast, University of El Segundo, IndustryNext, ElSegundo.xyz and Nouns Money as fictional settings and campaign ideas. Advertising copy is printed alongside the images; generated lettering is not authoritative. Nouns Money pieces are speculative collectible-art concepts with no financial promise, investment solicitation or official endorsement.</p><p>360 images does not mean 360 concepts. Each of 90 generation jobs produced four variations: 25 coastal jobs, 25 scene jobs and 40 distinct ad concepts. The six-stop edit is a way in; the contact sheet is the whole afternoon.</p></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="footer"><a class="wordmark" href="/">PointCast ↗</a><span>Filed under: a Saturday well imagined.</span><nav aria-label="PointCast"><a href="/archive">Archive</a><a href="/collect/">Collect</a><a href="/signature/">Signature Studio</a><a href="#cover-title">Back to the sunshine ↑</a></nav></footer>
    <dialog id="worlds-dialog" aria-labelledby="worlds-image-title" aria-describedby="worlds-image-meta">
      <div class="lightbox-toolbar"><span>THE SATURDAY CONTACT SHEET</span><button id="worlds-close" type="button" autofocus>Close <span aria-hidden="true">×</span></button></div>
      <div class="lightbox-content"><div class="lightbox-art"><img id="worlds-full-image" alt="" /><div class="lightbox-arrows"><button type="button" id="worlds-prev" aria-label="Previous image">←</button><button type="button" id="worlds-next" aria-label="Next image">→</button></div></div><div class="lightbox-info"><h2 id="worlds-image-title"></h2><p id="worlds-image-meta" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="worlds-image-copy"></div><p class="eyebrow">Four ways this world could go</p><div id="worlds-variants"></div><a id="worlds-open-image" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open optimized image ↗</a><p class="small-note">Speculative AI-generated artwork. Places and campaigns are imaginary; no real offer or endorsement.</p><p class="keyboard-hint">← → Browse · Esc Close</p></div></div>
    </dialog>
    <script id="worlds-data" type="application/json" set:html={JSON.stringify({images}).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')}></script>
    <script src="/saturday-worlds/saturday-worlds.js" is:inline defer></script>
  </body>
</html>
